      "message": "Let me make sure I understand correctly. New tests will default to `UNDEFINED`, unless the author specifies another version. (That is, some macros currently pass in a `CTSVersion()` at the end.)\n\nThen we\u0027ll change all the `UNDEFINED` to the current API level near the time of the release?\n\nBut we don\u0027t run tests that are `UNDEFINED`, meaning we won\u0027t run them until we manually change things.\n\nI think new tests should default to some `FUTURE` version, \u003e the current level, so that we\u0027ll run them. Then we can change all the `FUTURE` ones near release time.\n\nBut wait; at release time, we should have *zero* tests that are using the default, right? (Modulo any brand new tests written while the release is locked down but not out yet.) Maybe we should force all tests to have an explicit value - it might be easier to search and replace? i.e. I think it\u0027s going to be harder to find all uses of the macro that did *not* explicitly state the version and update them.",
